# RETRIM for the measured tract (NavyTower, MB 1843 + 1850): ONLY q moved: the card's three fold stiffnesses x 1.005307. Model-only: pressure held at the card's value,
# SUNG VCV /ala/ ON C3 (NavyTower, MB 27172, 27179, 27186; words lane, owner order 13205/13208): one render, the
# tract moves from DVTD subject 1's measured tense /a/ to the same subject's lateral /l/ and back to the /a/. No
# recording enters. Built by la/ala/mkword_ala.py from the C3 phrase /a/ card sh-ph-C3-a (md5 086b98585ace5cbe4d4cc20555899c88);
# the comments after this header describe that /a/ card.
# TRACT: Birkholz et al. 2020 (DVTD, CC0), the 3-D models' closed inner surfaces cut by the vowel cards' level cut.
#   /a/ (base, from 0 s, and the return): the /a/ card's own sections, s1-01-bahn-tense-a, 91 sections,
#   186.78 mm.
#   /l/ (keyframe l): s1-09-los-l (German "los"), 102 sections, 209.94 mm, first (glottal)
#   section 1.877 cm2, narrowest 0.955 cm2 (the two lateral channels summed); the
#   last two slabs merged under the flanged ceiling keeping volume and sum L/A (mergecut.py).
#   Limit: one area per level cannot carry the peak at 4407 Hz in s1-09's measured transfer function (FE 4425 Hz); the
#   /l/ cut matches its measured R1 239 Hz at -2.0 % and R2 1606 Hz at -1.6 %.
# TIMING (MB 27179, 27186): one AUTHORED time and two times READ FROM FIGURES of measured speech.
#   0.45 s is AUTHORED player timing: the end of V1, where the closing starts. No source gives it.
#   Closing, 0.45 to 0.628 s (0.178 s) in 27 steps: Geumann (2001), FIPKM 38, Fig. 6-13b, printed p. 303,
#   the jaw closing gesture from /a:/ into /l/, 'jaw dur minp2maxp': from the jaw's lowest position in V1 (minp) to its
#   highest in the consonant (maxp), Fig. 6-12, p. 302; one maxp per VCV, Fig. 6-4, p. 289. Split by consonant and
#   preceding vowel; 6 German speakers (5 male, 1 female), EMMA, N 152 for /l/ after /a/. The value is READ FROM THE
#   FIGURE, not printed: a 600 dpi render of PDF p. 39, the axis ticks fitted to 0.34 ms; mean 0.1781 s, the
#   figure's mean +- 1 SD bar about 0.058 s. Volume is not significant for the closing gesture (p. 302 text).
#   Opening, 0.628 to 0.723 s (0.095 s) in 27 steps, to the card's own /a/ shape: Geumann (2001), Fig. 6-25b,
#   printed p. 322, the jaw opening gesture from /l/ into /a:/ (maxp to minp), N 152. READ FROM THE FIGURE: a 600 dpi
#   render, the axis ticks fitted to 0.6 ms; mean 0.0949 s, SD about 0.048 s.
#   The closing ends where the opening starts: maxp is one point, so the /l/ shape is held for no time. Steps: plan
#   13292's rule, S = ceil(max |d ln A| / 0.1) on 102 equal sections, every section (27 and 27 over sections 1..).
#   Jaw only: the tongue tip closes and opens with the jaw for /l/ (Mooshammer, Geumann, Hoole, Alfonso, van Lieshout
#   and Fuchs (2003), ICPhS 15, Tab. 1, /l/ closing onset latency 3.2 ms (SD 29.1), opening onset latency -3.2 ms
#   (SD 17.8), printed).
#   CHECK, not an input: the same table's acoustic /l/ duration, 64.8 ms (SD 13.0), German /aCa/ at normal volume.
#   The render's acoustic /l/ interval is stamped in 38.8 to 90.8 ms (64.8 +- 2 x 13.0, MB 27179); a miss is
#   reported and licenses no change to any time here.
#   Limits: loud and normal speech pooled in both figures; jaw times applied to the whole tract's log-area morph;
#   speech, not singing; the stressed V1 / unstressed V2 of the corpus's /a:Ca:/, while both vowels here are sung at
#   one pressure and one note.
# PITCH: one fold; fold_tension carries the /l/ shape's own MODEL TRIM, stiffness x 1.02423 over the /a/ card's: x 1 through
#   V1, ramped to the trim over the closing and back to x 1 over the opening. The trim is FITTED to the model, not to a
#   recording: pressure held at the card's 489.687 Pa, set on the emergent f0 of one 1.5 s trial render of the /l/
#   shape on the same binary (straight tone, no flutter row, autocorrelation over 0.5-1.5 s) to within 3 cents of
#   130.81 Hz: x 1.024230 gave 130.81 Hz (-0.0 c, acf peak 0.992).
#   No value is taken from or fitted to a recording; the fold_tension trim is model-only, set on the emergent f0 of one trial render.
#   Vibrato and flutter keep the /a/ card's amplitudes throughout (factors 1).
# BREATH: the /a/ card's, unchanged (rise 0 to 0.15 s, 489.687 Pa held to 0.95 s, off at 1.05 s); V2 runs from
#   0.723 s to the release.
# Limits as in the one-render phrase: the island's zc and A_1 step to each shape's at its switch (not faded); the
# microphone, receiver and head sphere keep the /a/ card's mouth radius; frozen shapes moved, no volume source from
# moving walls; one flutter stream.
#   emergent f0 on a 1.5 s trial render with no flutter row (0.5-1.5 s, autocorrelation), to within 3 cents of the written note 130.81 Hz. No recording enters. Trace:
#     x 1.000000: f0 130.46 Hz (-4.6 c, acf peak 0.992) -> x 1.005307: f0 130.70 Hz (-1.4 c, acf peak 0.992)
# Voice performance: Tom et al. (1999) /a/ tract of a trained male singer, condition speech_comf, fold card of the licensed
# RETRIM (ALL-IN variant abcq, ChartreuseBass, owner GO 2 via MB 14813): the card is the abc card with ONLY q moved again.
#   The three fold stiffnesses are the abc card's values x 0.802536 (cumulative on the pack values x q of the abc card). Model-only: pressure held at the card's own value,
#   emergent f0 measured on a 1.5 s trial render (0.5-1.5 s, autocorrelation) of the straight card, iterated to within 3 cents of the written note. No recording enters.
#   Reason: fold_mapping bilateral (halved m, k, k_c in the full-gap coordinate) moved every emergent f0 sharp while the pack-value q had been trimmed per fold; this re-does the cards' own trim.
# two-mass pack, cited yielding wall, target note C3 (130.81 Hz). Every number below is cited. UNKNOWN marks a
# quantity no cited source gives; none is fitted to a recording.
#
# TRACT: Tom, K., Titze, I. R., Hoffman, E. A., and Story, B. H. (1999). 3-D vocal tract imaging and formant structure:
#   varying vocal register, pitch and loudness. NCVS Status and Progress Report 14:101-112 (National Center for Voice and
#   Speech; free PDF). Journal version: J. Acoust. Soc. Am. 109(2):742-747 (2001), doi:10.1121/1.1332380 (not read: paywalled).
#   Subject: one 45-year-old male, Western classical training (12 years as a baritone, 6 as a countertenor), EBCT (electron-beam
#   CT, 0.410 mm pixels, 3 mm axial slices), supine. Condition: spoken /a/, CHEST register, self-selected comfortable pitch B-flat2 (117 Hz) and loudness.
#   Areas: Table III column speech_comf, sections 1-44 glottis to lips, printed cm^2 digits scaled by e-4 (to m^2), transcribed
#   from the OCR of the scanned report and checked against the page image (tom1999-table-III-area-functions.tsv).
#   LENGTH: Table III is normalized to 17.46 cm (44 x 0.396825 cm). Table IV gives the measured length of this condition,
#   17.39 cm; the section length here is 17.39 cm / 44, which undoes the axial normalization (areas are unchanged by it).
#   LIMITS: (1) the sung conditions are FALSETTO, while the fold below is a modal two-mass card; (2) no piriform sinus: the
#   voice grammar has no side branch and the report does not print where the branch (Table V) attaches; (3) supine;
#   (4) one singer, vowel /a/ only.
#   Same-specimen check (computed, not measured): the authors' wave-reflection model with the sinus at 17.46 cm gives
#   F1-F4 543 993 2585 3747 Hz (Table VII). This file's passive tract (flanged, wall, no sinus) was predicted offline before the
#   render at F1-F5 562 1024 2641 3838 4646 Hz; the render sidecar (passive_tract_formants_hz) gives 563 1027 2643 3840 Hz.
#   The missing sinus is the main gap to Table VII (F1 +3.5 %).
#
# FOLD, FLOW LAW, WALL, GAS, MICROPHONE, LEVEL, MECHANICS: identical to story2008-a-C3-flanagan.performance (see its
#   header for every citation): Ishizaka-Flanagan two-mass pack in the Steinecke-Herzel form with the Poiseuille drop,
#   damping ratios 0.1 lower, 0.6 upper open, Ishizaka & Flanagan (1972) p. 1238, 1.0 more each while its section is shut;
#   RETRIM on this law: only q moved, pressure held, emergent f0 to within 3 cents of the note, no recording, q 0.544096 to 0.79141.
#   Trace:
#     q 0.544096: f0 113.80 Hz (-241.2 c) -> q 0.718938: f0 126.22 Hz (-61.8 c) -> q 0.79141: f0 130.79 Hz (-0.3 c)
#   Any other trace in this header is from an earlier law and ended at an earlier q.
#   Flanagan wall via Birkholz, Haesner and Kuerbis (ICASSP 2022), K ASSUMED;
#   saturated air at 310.15 K; flanged mouth; 0.30 m at 45 deg; 96 kHz mechanics clock.
# SUBGLOTTAL PRESSURE: AUTHORED PLAYER INPUT, 489.687 Pa: 900 Pa x the q 0.544096 of the previous trim, held when q moved on this law (tests/vowel_gates.rs vw-002 rule). Ramp 150 ms, hold, 150 ms release.
#   The 150 ms RISE is cited: Fant and Kruckenberg 2005, Interspeech, doi:10.21437/Interspeech.2005-425, Sec. 1 on Fig. 1: one male
#   speaker (a laryngologist) reading prose, true subglottal pressure by sonde: 'the duration of the rise to an initial value of the
#   order of 6-8 cm H2O is 120-180 ms' at the onset of a breath group; 150 ms is the centre of that range. LIMITS: speech, one subject,
#   not a singer's gesture, no adduction trajectory. Only the rise time is cited; the plateau P is this card's own authored value,
#   and their 3-5 and 6-8 cm H2O levels are NOT applied. The earlier 60 ms was authored. Steady state, and so the pitch trim, is unchanged.
# PITCH CONTROL (model-only objective): the three fold stiffnesses are the pack values x q = 0.79141. q was
#   iterated on the EMERGENT f0 of the radiated pressure (autocorrelation over 0.5-1.5 s of a 1.5 s trial render, same
#   binary) until it was within 3 cents of C3 = 130.81 Hz (A4 = 440 Hz). No recording enters. Trace
#   from the Story /a/ C3 q:
#     q 0.459164: f0 121.36 Hz (-129.8 c) -> q 0.533469: f0 129.68 Hz (-15.1 c) -> q 0.544097: f0 130.82 Hz (+0.1 c)
# ALL-IN variant (scratch copy, ChartreuseBass, owner order 14741, 2026-11-02). Original card unchanged in the shared tree.
# Added keys, each with its source (see make_allin_cards.py): `tension_modulation 5.85 0.09` vibrato (Larrouy-Maestri et al. 2014: 5.75-5.95 Hz, mean extent 139 cents; amplitude from the code's own 61.4 cents at 0.08), `tract_wall` the cited Flanagan/Birkholz wall where the card had none, mechanics ratio 4 (192 kHz, converged contact), `fold_mapping bilateral` (Ishizaka and Flanagan mirror pair, one fold of two), thermochemical ambient (NASA-9 + transport packs).
# The pitch was NOT retrimmed for these keys: the f0 against the nominal note is reported with each render.
frankensim-voice-performance-v1
# MEASURED TRACT A/B (NavyTower, MB 1843 + 1850; no landing, not a posted card): the tract is DVTD subject 1, s1-01-bahn-tense-a. Birkholz, Kuerbis, Stone, Haesner, Blandin, Fleischer, Sci. Data 7:255, 2020,
#   doi:10.1038/s41597-020-00597-w, CC0. A different man from the singer on this page, and speaking the subject's own vowels. The 3-D-printed model's STL was cut to a 1-D area function by a level cut made by the FrankenSim voice lane:
#   Laplace field on voxels, 0 at glottis, 1 at lips, walls no-flux; L A = V and L / A = dphi / flux per level. Printed area functions were not used. The last two slabs are merged into one section keeping their volume and sum L / A, since the raw last slab was over the flanged kernel ceiling of ka = 24 (mergecut.py). The section rows below replace the card's 44 Tom or Story rows; everything else in the card is as it was until the retrim moves q.
audio 48000 72000 4
full_scale_pa 8.0
ambient thermochemical 310.15 101325 mole 5 N2 0.73246735 O2 0.19649907 Ar 0.00876139 CO2 0.00029455 H2O 0.06197764
fold two_mass 0.000125 2.5e-05 51.0804872 5.10804872 15.9626119 0.1 3.57e-4 1.4e-2 2.5e-3
fold_damping_upper 0.6
termination flanged
# straight tone (VocalSet long_straight references): tension_modulation 5.85 0.09
fold_mapping bilateral
tract_wall 15 1.48e+06 1.6e4
tract_source birkholz-2020-dvtd-s1-01-bahn-tense-a-level-cut
tract_licence CC0 (DVTD, Birkholz et al. 2020); level cut by the FrankenSim voice lane
microphone 0.212132 0 0.212132 16 64 8000
subglottal 0 0
subglottal 0.15 489.687
subglottal 0.95 489.687
subglottal 1.05 0
