# JET NOISE, EXTRAPOLATION (SunnySnow, MB GO 16259): ONE added row. Page label (MB, verbatim): "constriction noise from a flue-jet measurement (Verge 1995: flue jet at a labium, slit 1 mm), applied to the glottal jet as an extrapolation; Stevens 1971 gives the form (a pressure source proportional to the pressure drop), not this constant". Numbers: gain 1.3e-3 of rho U_j^2/2 (0.92e-3 for the other analyser line width, +-3 dB), St_h 0.045-0.115 on the glottal gap, gate Re_h = Q/(L nu) >= 1700 (a flow threshold; about 44 % of the F4-a peak flow), U_j = Q/(L h) bounded by the Bernoulli speed of the drive. One value for every note; seed declared; nothing read from a recording.
jet_noise 20261103 1.3e-3 0.045 0.115 1700
# VIBRATO (sung phrases only; replaces this page's tension_flutter, the engine takes one gesture): 5.9 Hz, +-69.5 c, the means of 50 professional singers,
#   Larrouy-Maestri, Magis and Morsomme 2014, J Voice, doi:10.1016/j.jvoice.2013.10.019. a = (2^(69.5/1200) - 1) / 0.36548, this card's gain measured at 4 Hz, 0.02, once, not iterated.
tension_modulation 5.9 0.11208
# FAST PITCH ROW UNDER VIBRATO (MB 3377): the page card fr-C3-a's second row, seed 1, F 20 BW 20, sd_rel 0.005361, copied as this card's only flutter row. Its size is the straight-tone size of Ternstrom and Friberg 1989 Fig. 5 applied under vibrato: no print for fast movement under vibrato was read. The engine adds it to the vibrato on one tension, 1 + a sin + y, a choice of this card; no print sets it. No recording enters.
tension_flutter 1 20 20 0.005361
# pulse_shimmer (MB 3551, 3576, 3719): a per-cycle gain on the wave the tract receives, a new g at each opening of the glottis.
# Size: local shimmer 1.28 % for classical singing students (n 65), Yoo, Ahn, Kwon and Jeong 2002, Communication Sciences
# and Disorders 7(2):126-134, read from the abstract only; whether the /a/ was sung or spoken is not stated there, and the
# tracker floor was not taken out. For independent normal gains local shimmer is 2 sd / sqrt(pi), so sd = 1.28 % x
# sqrt(pi) / 2 = 1.1344 %. Seed 6 on every card; the row has its own stream kernel.
pulse_shimmer 6 0.011344
keyframe l source birkholz-2020-dvtd-s1-09-los-l-level-cut
